    {
      "name": "Senior 2 (S2)",
      "subjects": [
        {
          "name": "Mathematics",
          "description": "Advanced algebra, functions, geometry, trigonometry and vectors",
          "units": [
            {
              "name": "Unit 1: Algebraic Expressions",
              "lessons": [
                "Expansion of algebraic expressions",
                "Factorization techniques",
                "Algebraic fractions",
                "Simplification of rational expressions",
                "Applications of algebraic expressions"
              ],
              "lessons_content": [
                {
                  "objectives": "By the end of this lesson, you should be able to: \n- Expand expressions with brackets\n- Use the distributive property\n- Simplify expanded expressions",
                  "reading": "When we expand algebraic expressions, we remove brackets by multiplying each term inside by the term outside. This is called the distributive property.\n\nFor example: 3(x + 4) = 3 × x + 3 × 4 = 3x + 12\n\nIn Rwanda, if a farmer sells 2 bags of rice at (10,000 + d) RWF each, total = 2(10,000 + d) = 20,000 + 2d RWF.\n\nKey rule: a(b + c) = ab + ac\n\nIf the sign outside is negative, change the signs inside: -2(x - 5) = -2x + 10",
                  "examples": "Example 1: Expand 4(x + 7)\nSolution:\n4(x + 7) = 4 × x + 4 × 7 = 4x + 28\nAnswer: 4x + 28\n\nExample 2: Expand -3(2x - 6)\nSolution:\n-3(2x - 6) = -3 × 2x - (-3) × 6 = -6x + 18\nAnswer: -6x + 18\n\nExample 3: Expand and simplify 2(x + 5) + 3(x - 2)\n= 2x + 10 + 3x - 6 = 5x + 4",
                  "practice": "1. (Easy) Expand: 5(x + 3)\n2. (Easy) Expand: 2(3y - 4)\n3. (Medium) Expand and simplify: 4(a + 2) + 3(a - 1)\n4. (Medium) Expand: -2(5x - 3)\n5. (Hard) A shop sells 'm' mangoes at (200 + 50x) RWF each. Write and expand an expression for the total cost of 5 mangoes.",
                  "practice_answers": "1. 5x + 15\n2. 6y - 8\n3. 7a + 5\n4. -10x + 6\n5. 5(200 + 50x) = 1,000 + 250x RWF",
                  "summary": "* Expansion removes brackets by multiplying each term inside\n* Distributive property: a(b + c) = ab + ac\n* With a negative sign outside, change the signs inside\n* Always simplify by collecting like terms",
                  "quiz": {
                    "question": "Expand: 3(x + 4)",
                    "options": {
                      "A": "3x + 4",
                      "B": "3x + 7",
                      "C": "3x + 12",
                      "D": "x + 12"
                    },
                    "answer": "C"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "objectives": "By the end of this lesson, you should be able to: \n- Factor algebraic expressions by finding common factors\n- Write expressions as products of factors\n- Check factorization by expanding",
                  "reading": "Factorization is the opposite of expansion. We find a common factor that divides all terms and put it outside brackets.\n\n6x + 9 = 3(2x + 3) because 3 divides both 6x and 9.\n\nIn Rwanda, if 2 farmers each bring 5 kg of beans and 3 kg of maize, total = 2(5 + 3) = 16 kg.\n\nSteps:\n1. Find the HCF of all terms\n2. Write the HCF outside the bracket\n3. Divide each term and write inside\n4. Check by expanding!",
                  "examples": "Example 1: Factorize 8x + 12\nSolution:\nHCF of 8 and 12 is 4\n8x ÷ 4 = 2x, 12 ÷ 4 = 3\n8x + 12 = 4(2x + 3)\nCheck: 4(2x + 3) = 8x + 12 ✓\n\nExample 2: Factorize 15y - 10\nHCF = 5, so 5(3y - 2)\n\nExample 3: Factorize 6x² + 9x\nHCF = 3x, so 3x(2x + 3)",
                  "practice": "1. (Easy) Factorize: 10x + 15\n2. (Easy) Factorize: 8y - 12\n3. (Medium) Factorize: 12a + 18b\n4. (Medium) Factorize: 7x² + 14x\n5. (Hard) Factorize fully: 16x²y - 8xy²",
                  "practice_answers": "1. 5(2x + 3)\n2. 4(2y - 3)\n3. 6(2a + 3b)\n4. 7x(x + 2)\n5. 8xy(2x - y)",
                  "summary": "* Factorization is the reverse of expansion\n* Find the HCF of all terms\n* Put the HCF outside brackets and divide each term\n* Always check by expanding",
                  "quiz": {
                    "question": "Factorize: 12x + 18",
                    "options": {
                      "A": "2(6x + 9)",
                      "B": "3(4x + 6)",
                      "C": "6(2x + 3)",
                      "D": "12(x + 1)"
                    },
                    "answer": "C"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "objectives": "By the end of this lesson, you should be able to: \n- Add and subtract algebraic fractions\n- Simplify algebraic fractions\n- Find common denominators",
                  "reading": "Algebraic fractions work just like numerical fractions - you need a common denominator.\n\nx/3 + x/6 = 2x/6 + x/6 = 3x/6 = x/2\n\nIn Rwanda, if ⅓ of a field grows maize and ¼ grows beans, total = 4/12 + 3/12 = 7/12.\n\nSteps:\n1. Find the LCD\n2. Convert each fraction\n3. Add/subtract numerators\n4. Simplify",
                  "examples": "Example 1: Simplify: x/5 + x/10\nLCD = 10, so 2x/10 + x/10 = 3x/10\n\nExample 2: Simplify: 2x/3 - x/4\nLCD = 12, so 8x/12 - 3x/12 = 5x/12\n\nExample 3: Simplify: 3/x + 2/x²\nLCD = x², so 3x/x² + 2/x² = (3x + 2)/x²",
                  "practice": "1. (Easy) Simplify: x/2 + x/2\n2. (Easy) Simplify: 2y/5 + y/5\n3. (Medium) Simplify: x/3 + x/6\n4. (Medium) Simplify: 3a/4 - a/8\n5. (Hard) Simplify: 2/x + 3/x²",
                  "practice_answers": "1. x\n2. 3y/5\n3. x/2\n4. 5a/8\n5. (2x + 3)/x²",
                  "summary": "* Algebraic fractions follow the same rules as number fractions\n* Find the LCD before adding or subtracting\n* Convert each fraction to the common denominator\n* Add/subtract numerators and simplify",
                  "quiz": {
                    "question": "Simplify: x/4 + x/8",
                    "options": {
                      "A": "x/12",
                      "B": "2x/12",
                      "C": "3x/8",
                      "D": "x/4"
                    },
                    "answer": "C"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "objectives": "By the end of this lesson, you should be able to: \n- Simplify rational expressions\n- Cancel common factors\n- Identify undefined values",
                  "reading": "A rational expression is a fraction where numerator/denominator are algebraic. Simplify by cancelling common factors.\n\n(6x)/(9x²) = (2)/(3x)\n\nIn Rwanda, if a farmer has (x² + x) hectares divided into (x + 1) plots, each plot = x(x+1)/(x+1) = x hectares.\n\nImportant: Denominator cannot be zero. So (x + 2)/(x - 3) is undefined when x = 3.",
                  "examples": "Example 1: Simplify: (12x³)/(8x²)\nDivide by 4x²: = 3x/2\n\nExample 2: Simplify: (x² - 9)/(x + 3)\nFactor: (x+3)(x-3)/(x+3) = x - 3, x ≠ -3\n\nExample 3: When is (x + 5)/(x - 2) undefined?\nx - 2 = 0, so x = 2",
                  "practice": "1. (Easy) Simplify: (10x)/(15)\n2. (Easy) Simplify: (6y²)/(3y)\n3. (Medium) Simplify: (x² - 4)/(x - 2)\n4. (Medium) State when (x + 1)/(x - 5) is undefined\n5. (Hard) Simplify: (x² + 3x)/(x² - 9)",
                  "practice_answers": "1. 2x/3\n2. 2y\n3. x + 2\n4. x = 5\n5. x/(x - 3), x ≠ 3",
                  "summary": "* Simplify by cancelling common factors\n* Factor numerator and denominator first if needed\n* Undefined when denominator = 0\n* State any restrictions on the variable",
                  "quiz": {
                    "question": "Simplify: (8x²)/(4x)",
                    "options": {
                      "A": "2x",
                      "B": "4x",
                      "C": "2x²",
                      "D": "8x"
                    },
                    "answer": "A"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "objectives": "By the end of this lesson, you should be able to: \n- Use algebraic expressions in real problems\n- Apply expansion and factorization in context\n- Model daily situations with algebra",
                  "reading": "Algebra solves real problems!\n\nIn Rwanda: a farmer calculates fertilizer needs, a business figures profit, a family plans a budget.\n\nTranslate words into algebra:\n\"A cow costs 500,000 RWF. A goat costs 80,000 RWF. x cows and y goats: cost = 500,000x + 80,000y RWF\"\n\nAlways define variables first!",
                  "examples": "Example 1: A school buys x desks at 25,000 RWF each and y chairs at 12,000 RWF each. Total cost?\nCost = 25,000x + 12,000y RWF\nFor 20 desks, 40 chairs: 25,000(20) + 12,000(40) = 980,000 RWF\n\nExample 2: Field length = (x + 5) m, width = (x - 2) m. Area?\n(x+5)(x-2) = x² + 3x - 10 m²\nIf x = 10: Area = 120 m²",
                  "practice": "1. (Easy) A pen costs 500 RWF and a book 2,000 RWF. Cost of p pens and b books?\n2. (Easy) A farmer has x cows, sells 5. How many left?\n3. (Medium) Taxi: 1,000 RWF base + 500 RWF per km. Cost for d km? For 8 km?\n4. (Medium) Garden length = (2x + 3) m, width = (x + 1) m. Find area (expanded).\n5. (Hard) A trader buys 100 kg rice at x RWF/kg and 50 kg beans at y RWF/kg. Total cost? If x = 800, y = 1,200, find total.",
                  "practice_answers": "1. 500p + 2,000b RWF\n2. x - 5\n3. 1,000 + 500d RWF; 5,000 RWF\n4. 2x² + 5x + 3 m²\n5. 100x + 50y RWF; 140,000 RWF",
                  "summary": "* Translate word problems into algebraic expressions\n* Define variables clearly\n* Use expansion and factorization to simplify\n* Substitute values to find numerical answers",
                  "quiz": {
                    "question": "A worker earns 3,000 RWF per hour. Expression for h hours:",
                    "options": {
                      "A": "3,000 + h",
                      "B": "3,000/h",
                      "C": "3,000h",
                      "D": "h - 3,000"
                    },
                    "answer": "C"
                  }
                }
              ],
