            {
              "name": "Unit 3: Sequences and Patterns",
              "lessons": [
                "Arithmetic sequences",
                "Geometric sequences",
                "Finding the nth term",
                "Sum of sequences",
                "Real-life applications of sequences"
              ],
              "lessons_content": [
                {
                  "objectives": "By the end of this lesson, you should be able to: \n- Identify arithmetic sequences\n- Find the common difference\n- Extend arithmetic sequences",
                  "reading": "Arithmetic sequence: constant difference (d) between consecutive terms.\n\nExample: 3, 7, 11, 15, 19... d = 4\n\nIn Rwanda: saving 5,000 RWF weekly: 5,000, 10,000, 15,000...\nFarmer plants 10 more trees each year: 50, 60, 70...\n\nTo find next term: add d.\nTo find d: subtract any term from the next.",
                  "examples": "Example 1: 12, 17, 22, 27... d = 5. Next: 32, 37\n\nExample 2: 20, 16, 12, 8... d = -4. Next: 4, 0\n\nExample 3: Farmer saves 3,000 RWF week 1, 500 more each week. Week 5? 3,000, 3,500, 4,000, 4,500, 5,000 RWF",
                  "practice": "1. (Easy) Find d: 5, 9, 13, 17...\n2. (Easy) Next two: 30, 27, 24, 21...\n3. (Medium) Is 1, 4, 9, 16... arithmetic? Explain.\n4. (Medium) Student reads 10, 15, 20, 25 pages/day. Day 6?\n5. (Hard) Start 100, subtract 8 each time. 5th term? 10th term?",
                  "practice_answers": "1. d = 4\n2. 18, 15\n3. No, differences 3,5,7 not constant\n4. 35 pages\n5. 5th: 68, 10th: 28",
                  "summary": "* Arithmetic: constant difference between terms\n* d = term - previous term\n* d > 0: increases, d < 0: decreases\n* Add d to find next term",
                  "quiz": {
                    "question": "Common difference of 7, 12, 17, 22... is:",
                    "options": {
                      "A": "3",
                      "B": "4",
                      "C": "5",
                      "D": "6"
                    },
                    "answer": "C"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "objectives": "By the end of this lesson, you should be able to: \n- Identify geometric sequences\n- Find the common ratio\n- Distinguish arithmetic from geometric",
                  "reading": "Geometric sequence: each term = previous × constant ratio (r).\n\nExample: 3, 6, 12, 24... r = 2\n\nIn Rwanda: savings with 10% interest: 100,000, 110,000, 121,000...\nBacteria doubling each hour.\n\nTo find next term: multiply by r.\n|r| > 1: grows. |r| < 1: shrinks.",
                  "examples": "Example 1: 2, 6, 18, 54... r = 3. Next: 162, 486\n\nExample 2: 100, 50, 25, 12.5... r = 0.5 (halving)\n\nExample 3: 5, 10, 20, 40 arithmetic or geometric?\nArithmetic check: 10-5=5, 20-10=10 not constant\nGeometric check: 10/5=2, 20/10=2, 40/20=2 constant\nSo geometric, r = 2",
                  "practice": "1. (Easy) Find r: 3, 9, 27, 81...\n2. (Easy) Next two: 64, 32, 16, 8...\n3. (Medium) Is 4, 8, 12, 16 arithmetic or geometric?\n4. (Medium) Harvest increases 50%/year. Year 1: 200 kg. Year 3?\n5. (Hard) Population 1,000 doubles every 3 years. First 4 terms and r.",
                  "practice_answers": "1. r = 3\n2. 4, 2\n3. Arithmetic, d = 4\n4. Year 2: 300, Year 3: 450 kg\n5. 1,000, 2,000, 4,000, 8,000; r = 2",
                  "summary": "* Geometric: each term = previous × r\n* r = term ÷ previous term\n* |r| > 1: grows, |r| < 1: shrinks\n* Check both difference and ratio to identify type",
                  "quiz": {
                    "question": "Common ratio of 2, 10, 50, 250... is:",
                    "options": {
                      "A": "3",
                      "B": "4",
                      "C": "5",
                      "D": "8"
                    },
                    "answer": "C"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "objectives": "By the end of this lesson, you should be able to: \n- Find the nth term of an arithmetic sequence\n- Use formula a_n = a_1 + (n-1)d\n- Find specific terms",
                  "reading": "Formula: a_n = a_1 + (n - 1)d\n\na_n = nth term\na_1 = first term\nn = position\nd = common difference\n\nIn Rwanda: business starts with 50 customers + 10/month.\na_12 = 50 + (12-1)10 = 50 + 110 = 160 customers after 12 months!",
                  "examples": "Example 1: 20th term of 3, 7, 11, 15...\na_1 = 3, d = 4, n = 20\na_20 = 3 + (19)4 = 3 + 76 = 79\n\nExample 2: 15th term of 50, 46, 42, 38...\na_1 = 50, d = -4\na_15 = 50 + (14)(-4) = 50 - 56 = -6\n\nExample 3: Save 500 RWF week 1, +200/week. Week 10? a_10 = 500 + 9(200) = 2,300 RWF",
                  "practice": "1. (Easy) 10th term of 2, 5, 8, 11...\n2. (Easy) 8th term of 100, 90, 80, 70...\n3. (Medium) a_1 = 7, d = 3. 25th term?\n4. (Medium) Farmer plants 20 trees year 1, +15/year. Year 7?\n5. (Hard) Which term = 100 in 4, 10, 16, 22...?",
                  "practice_answers": "1. 29\n2. 30\n3. 79\n4. 110 trees\n5. 100 = 4 + (n-1)6, n = 17",
                  "summary": "* Formula: a_n = a_1 + (n-1)d\n* Identify a_1, d, n first\n* Can also find n if a_n is known",
                  "quiz": {
                    "question": "12th term of 5, 9, 13, 17... is:",
                    "options": {
                      "A": "45",
                      "B": "47",
                      "C": "49",
                      "D": "51"
                    },
                    "answer": "C"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "objectives": "By the end of this lesson, you should be able to: \n- Find sum of arithmetic terms\n- Use S_n = n/2(a_1 + a_n)\n- Apply sum formula in real life",
                  "reading": "Sum formula: S_n = n/2(a_1 + a_n)\n\nPairs first and last: each pair has same sum!\n\nIn Rwanda: farmer saves 10,000 RWF month 1, +1,000/month. Total after 12 months? Instead of adding 12 terms, use the formula!",
                  "examples": "Example 1: Sum of 1 + 2 + 3 + ... + 100\nS_100 = 100/2(1+100) = 50(101) = 5,050\n\nExample 2: First 20 terms of 3, 7, 11, 15...\na_20 = 3 + 19(4) = 79\nS_20 = 20/2(3+79) = 10(82) = 820\n\nExample 3: Save 500, 700, 900... in 10 weeks.\na_10 = 500 + 9(200) = 2,300\nS_10 = 10/2(500+2,300) = 5(2,800) = 14,000 RWF",
                  "practice": "1. (Easy) Sum 1+2+...+10\n2. (Easy) Sum 2+4+6+...+20\n3. (Medium) Sum first 15 terms: 5, 9, 13, 17...\n4. (Medium) Harvest 100, 120, 140... in 8 weeks. Total?\n5. (Hard) Sum of multiples of 3 from 3 to 99.",
                  "practice_answers": "1. 55\n2. 110\n3. a_15 = 61, S_15 = 495\n4. 1,360 kg\n5. n = 33, S_33 = 1,683",
                  "summary": "* S_n = n/2(a_1 + a_n)\n* First find a_n using nth term formula\n* Useful for finding totals over time",
                  "quiz": {
                    "question": "Sum of 5 + 10 + 15 + ... + 50 is:",
                    "options": {
                      "A": "255",
                      "B": "275",
                      "C": "300",
                      "D": "325"
                    },
                    "answer": "B"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "objectives": "By the end of this lesson, you should be able to: \n- Apply sequences to real problems\n- Identify patterns in daily life\n- Use sequences for planning and prediction",
                  "reading": "Sequences around us in Rwanda:\n- Saving money: arithmetic deposits\n- Population growth: geometric patterns\n- Crop yields increasing by fixed amounts\n- Business profits growing by percentages\n\nKey: Is change by addition (arithmetic) or multiplication (geometric)?",
                  "examples": "Example 1: Farmer has 5 cows, buys 3/year. After 8 years?\na_9 = 5 + 8(3) = 29 cows. Total cost: 24 × 400,000 = 9,600,000 RWF\n\nExample 2: Phone 150,000 RWF loses 10%/year. Value after 3 years?\na_4 = 150,000(0.9)³ = 109,350 RWF\n\nExample 3: School 200 students, +25/year. When reach 350?\n200 + (n-1)25 = 350, n = 7 (6 years from now)",
                  "practice": "1. (Easy) Shop sells 20, 25, 30 items/day. Day 10?\n2. (Easy) Bacteria 100, doubles/hour. After 5 hours?\n3. (Medium) Trees: 50, 65, 80... Total in 10 years?\n4. (Medium) Salary 200,000 RWF + 5%/year. Year 4?\n5. (Hard) Save 5,000 RWF month 1, +500/month. Months to reach 150,000 RWF?",
                  "practice_answers": "1. 65 items\n2. 3,200\n3. 1,175 trees\n4. ~231,525 RWF\n5. S_n = n/2(2(5000)+(n-1)500) = 150,000; n ≈ 17 months",
                  "summary": "* Identify if pattern is arithmetic or geometric\n* Arithmetic: constant difference\n* Geometric: constant ratio\n* Use formulas to predict and plan",
                  "quiz": {
                    "question": "Population 500 grows by 20/year. After 10 years:",
                    "options": {
                      "A": "520",
                      "B": "600",
                      "C": "700",
                      "D": "1,000"
                    },
                    "answer": "C"
                  }
                }
              ],
              "previous_answers": "Unit 2 Quiz Answers: 1-A, 2-B, 3-C, 4-A, 5-B, 6-A, 7-B, 8-C, 9-B, 10-C",
