            {
              "name": "Unit 7: Vectors",
              "lessons": [
                "Vector concepts (magnitude, direction)",
                "Vector addition and subtraction",
                "Scalar multiplication",
                "Position vectors",
                "Applications of vectors"
              ],
              "lessons_content": [
                {
                  "objectives": "By the end of this lesson, you should be able to: \n- Understand vector concepts\n- Represent vectors as directed segments\n- Find magnitude and direction",
                  "reading": "Vector = magnitude (size) + direction.\nScalar = only magnitude.\n\n5 km = scalar. 5 km East = vector.\n\nIn Rwanda: \"Walk 200 m to market\" (scalar). \"Walk 200 m East to market\" (vector).\n\nWe draw vectors as arrows: length = magnitude, arrowhead = direction.\n\nWritten as: → or v or column (x, y).",
                  "examples": "Example 1: Car travels 40 km East. Vector? Yes! Magnitude 40 km, direction East.\n\nExample 2: Draw vector 5 units North. Arrow 5 units pointing up.\n\nExample 3: Bird 10 m at 30°. Components: (10cos30°, 10sin30°) = (8.66, 5)",
                  "practice": "1. (Easy) Is \"30 kg\" vector or scalar?\n2. (Easy) Is \"20 m North\" vector or scalar?\n3. (Medium) Vector components (3,4). Find magnitude.\n4. (Medium) 6 km East + 8 km North. Total displacement?\n5. (Hard) Vector magnitude 10 at 60°. Find components.",
                  "practice_answers": "1. Scalar (no direction)\n2. Vector (has direction)\n3. Magnitude = 5\n4. Magnitude = 10 km, NE\n5. Horizontal=5, vertical=8.66",
                  "summary": "* Vectors: magnitude AND direction\n* Scalars: only magnitude\n* Draw as arrows\n* Components: break into x and y parts",
                  "quiz": {
                    "question": "Which is a vector?",
                    "options": {
                      "A": "25 kg",
                      "B": "100 RWF",
                      "C": "30°C",
                      "D": "50 km/h East"
                    },
                    "answer": "D"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "objectives": "By the end of this lesson, you should be able to: \n- Add vectors (tip-to-tail)\n- Subtract vectors\n- Find resultant vector",
                  "reading": "Tip-to-tail method:\n1. Draw first vector\n2. Draw second from tip of first\n3. Resultant: tail of first to tip of second\n\n3 km East + 4 km North = 5 km Northeast\n\nComponents: a+b = (x₁+x₂, y₁+y₂)\n\nSubtraction: a-b = a+(-b)",
                  "examples": "Example 1: 3 right + 4 up. Resultant mag = 5, direction ≈ 53°\n\nExample 2: a=(2,3), b=(4,1). a+b = (6,4)\n\nExample 3: 10 km East + 5 km West = 5 km East",
                  "practice": "1. (Easy) 3 right + 2 right = ?\n2. (Easy) a=(1,2), b=(3,4). a+b?\n3. (Medium) 5 km N + 12 km E. Resultant magnitude?\n4. (Medium) Plane 200 km N + 150 km S. Resultant?\n5. (Hard) a=(3,-2), b=(-1,5). a+b and magnitude.",
                  "practice_answers": "1. 5 right\n2. (4, 6)\n3. 13 km\n4. 50 km North\n5. (2, 3), magnitude=√13≈3.6",
                  "summary": "* Tip-to-tail: connect vectors\n* Resultant: start to finish\n* Add components separately\n* Opposite directions cancel",
                  "quiz": {
                    "question": "Add (2,3) and (4,1). Resultant:",
                    "options": {
                      "A": "(6,4)",
                      "B": "(4,6)",
                      "C": "(8,3)",
                      "D": "(2,2)"
                    },
                    "answer": "A"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "objectives": "By the end of this lesson, you should be able to: \n- Multiply a vector by a scalar\n- Understand how scalar multiplication changes vectors\n- Apply to real situations",
                  "reading": "kv = (kx, ky)\nk > 1: longer\n0<k<1: shorter\nk<0: reverse direction\n\nv = 60 km/h East, 2v = 120 km/h East\nv = 100 km/h North, -v = 100 km/h South\n\nMagnitude multiplies by |k|, direction stays same (unless k negative).",
                  "examples": "Example 1: v=(3,4), 2v=(6,8). |v|=5, |2v|=10\n\nExample 2: v=5 km East. -v=5 km West. 0.5v=2.5 km East\n\nExample 3: f=(10,20) N. 3f=(30,60) N (three times the force)",
                  "practice": "1. (Easy) v=(2,5). 3v?\n2. (Easy) v=3 km North. -v?\n3. (Medium) a=(1,-2). 4a and |4a|?\n4. (Medium) Vector mag 8, ×0.25. New mag?\n5. (Hard) v=(6,8). 1.5v. Show |1.5v|=1.5|v|",
                  "practice_answers": "1. (6, 15)\n2. 3 km South\n3. (4,-8), |4a|=√80≈8.94\n4. 2\n5. (9,12), |v|=10, |1.5v|=15=1.5×10",
                  "summary": "* kv = (kx, ky)\n* k>1: longer, 0<k<1: shorter, k<0: reverse\n* Magnitude ×|k|, direction same (or opposite)",
                  "quiz": {
                    "question": "v=(3,4). 2v =",
                    "options": {
                      "A": "(6,6)",
                      "B": "(5,6)",
                      "C": "(6,8)",
                      "D": "(9,12)"
                    },
                    "answer": "C"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "objectives": "By the end of this lesson, you should be able to: \n- Understand position vectors\n- Find the vector between two points\n- Use vectors to describe positions",
                  "reading": "Position vector: OA = coordinates of A from origin.\n\nVector AB = OB - OA = (x_b - x_a, y_b - y_a)\n\n\"From market A, school is 2 km East, 1 km North\": AB = (2, 1)\n\nBA = -AB (opposite direction).",
                  "examples": "Example 1: A(2,3). OA = (2,3)\n\nExample 2: A(1,2), B(5,7). AB = (4,5)\n\nExample 3: A(3,-1), B(-2,4). AB = (-5,5), BA = (5,-5) = -AB",
                  "practice": "1. (Easy) Position vector of (4,6)\n2. (Easy) A(1,1), B(4,5). AB?\n3. (Medium) A(-2,3), B(3,-2). AB and magnitude?\n4. (Medium) OA=(2,4), OB=(7,6). AB?\n5. (Hard) A(1,2), B(4,6), C(7,10). Show AB=BC. What does this mean?",
                  "practice_answers": "1. (4, 6)\n2. (3, 4)\n3. (5,-5), mag=√50≈7.07\n4. (5, 2)\n5. AB=(3,4)=BC; A,B,C are collinear",
                  "summary": "* OA = point's coordinates from origin\n* AB = OB - OA\n* BA = -AB",
                  "quiz": {
                    "question": "A(1,2), B(4,6). AB =",
                    "options": {
                      "A": "(3,4)",
                      "B": "(4,3)",
                      "C": "(-3,-4)",
                      "D": "(5,8)"
                    },
                    "answer": "A"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "objectives": "By the end of this lesson, you should be able to: \n- Apply vectors to real problems\n- Use vectors in navigation\n- Solve displacement and velocity problems",
                  "reading": "Real vector uses:\n1. Navigation: plane velocity + wind = resultant\n2. Forces: net force = vector sum\n3. Sports: ball velocity decomposed into components\n4. GPS: position vectors\n\nSteps: draw diagram, break into components, add, find resultant.",
                  "examples": "Example 1: Boat 4 m/s East, current 3 m/s South. Resultant = 5 m/s at 36.9° S of E\n\nExample 2: Car 5 km East + 12 km North. Displacement = 13 km at 67.4° from East\n\nExample 3: Forces 10 N East + 5 N West = 5 N East",
                  "practice": "1. (Easy) Plane 300 km N + 400 km E. Distance from start?\n2. (Easy) 8 N East + 2 N East. Net force?\n3. (Medium) Boat 6 m/s across, current 4 m/s. Resultant velocity?\n4. (Medium) Forces 5 N N + 12 N E. Net force magnitude and direction.\n5. (Hard) Plane 200 km/h N, wind 50 km/h E. Actual velocity?",
                  "practice_answers": "1. 500 km\n2. 10 N East\n3. ≈ 7.2 m/s, θ≈33.7°\n4. 13 N, θ≈67.4° from East\n5. ≈ 206 km/h, θ≈14° E of N",
                  "summary": "* Vectors model navigation, forces, motion\n* Add by components or tip-to-tail\n* Use Pythagoras and trig for resultant",
                  "quiz": {
                    "question": "3 N East + 4 N North. Net magnitude:",
                    "options": {
                      "A": "5 N",
                      "B": "7 N",
                      "C": "12 N",
                      "D": "1 N"
                    },
                    "answer": "A"
                  }
                }
              ],
